  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "One mole of a monoatomic gas is mixed with three moles of a diatomic gas. The molecular specific heat of mixture at constant volume is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>; then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> will be _____ . (Assume that the given diatomic gas has no vibrational mode.)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Molecular specific heat at constant volume in&nbsp;terms of degrees of freedom&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>Molecular specific heat of mixture at constant volume is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>mix</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
